+### Release readiness ownership
+
+The current agent owns full release readiness across macOS, Linux, and Windows. Run the complete macOS readiness pass and its declared Linux containers, then run the complete native Windows pass through the `windows-ssh` skill. Do not stop at local success or hand Windows testing to another agent by default. Follow `docs/guides/deployment-readiness-playbook.md` and `docs/guides/windows-deployment-readiness-playbook.md` for the same candidate revision. Preserve remote isolation and the user's installation. Report unavailable access or required desktop-only evidence as blockers, not passes. Cross-compilation does not prove runtime behavior. This requirement applies to chat agents, development-mode agents, and release skills.
